speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, considering the continuing attacks that the Minister of Finance of Canada is launching against the government of Quebec;
Considering that in doing so he maintains a climate of suspicions which greatly affects the normal progress not only of Quebec but of Canada as a whole;
Considering that such an important position as the one he occupies requires, in addition to genuine competence, statesmanship so as to stay above contingencies of narrow and sterile partisan spirit;
Considering that his action is causing prejudices to those who sincerely want harmony in a renewed Canada, I move, seconded by the hon. member for Rimouski (Mr. Allard):
That the House ask the Prime Minister to transfer his Minister of Finance to a position more in line with his capacities.
